{"name":"Superstitious","hex":"#ac91b5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"superstitious","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Susceptible to superstitions.","Arising from or having the character of superstitions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/superstitious"}],"entries":[{"title":"Superstitious (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Superstitious\" is a 1988 single released by the Swedish rock band Europe. It was the first single released from the album Out of This World. It performed moderately well, peaking at #31 on the US Billboard Hot 100, #9 on the Mainstream Rock Tracks and #34 on the UK Singles Chart. It was the last song by Europe to chart on the US Hot 100."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a2/Europe_Superstitious.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superstitious_(song)"},{"title":"Superstitious (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Superstitious is a 1995 horror novel by author R. L. Stine. This was the first adult novel by Stine, most famous for writing children's fiction such as the Goosebumps series. This book deals with Sara Morgan, who falls in love with Liam O’Connor. It was published on September 14, 1995 by Grand Central Publishing in the United States."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Superstitious_book.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superstitious_(novel)"},{"title":"Superstition","blocks":[{"text":"A superstition is any belief or practice considered by non-practitioners to be irrational or supernatural. It is commonly applied to beliefs and practices surrounding luck, fate, magic, amulets, astrology, fortune telling, spirits, and certain paranormal entities, particularly the belief that future events can be foretold by specific unrelated prior events."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Salem_witch2.jpg/330px-Salem_witch2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superstition"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/WeirdTalesv36n2pg043_Superstitions_and_Taboos.png/500px-WeirdTalesv36n2pg043_Superstitions_and_Taboos.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/WeirdTalesv36n2pg043_Superstitions_and_Taboos.png/1280px-WeirdTalesv36n2pg043_Superstitions_and_Taboos.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/WeirdTalesv36n2pg043_Superstitions_and_Taboos.png/500px-WeirdTalesv36n2pg043_Superstitions_and_Taboos.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Examples of superstitions and taboos from a November 1941 issue of Weird Tales","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWeirdTalesv36n2pg043_Superstitions_and_Taboos.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_cat_crossing_your_path.jpg/500px-Black_cat_crossing_your_path.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_cat_crossing_your_path.jpg/1280px-Black_cat_crossing_your_path.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_cat_crossing_your_path.jpg/500px-Black_cat_crossing_your_path.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A black cat","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_cat_crossing_your_path.jpg"}],"sounds":{"superstitious":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/En-us-superstitious.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/52/En-us-superstitious.ogg/En-us-superstitious.ogg.mp3"}]}}}